The strategy I always use is to use my first several prayers for
sustenance only.  I collect all the food rations, and save them
for when I've got bigger problems.  If I'm low on hit points,
I'll dally awhile to heal, maybe let my pet get some combat practice.
If I get bitten by a lycanthrope, I grin and bear it until I'm
weak from hunger also.  Usually my God likes me enough to fix
both of those problems at once.

It seems that the amount of time it takes to get from a
"content stomach" down to "weak" or "fainting" is enough
for the mandatory delay between prayers.  Eating corpses
always helps to delay the prayer / casting lots of spells
interferes (so I make sure I eat something after every
other spell or so).

By saving all my food for later, when things really get
hairy, I can safely pray for hit points, etc. without
having to worry about my stomach.

Just for curiosity --- what other strategies to people
use to maximize their use of prayers?  I'm primarily
interested in what you do before you find your altars
where the priorities change drastically.

